      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a quick-start guide for the field techs:\n\n**Installing the Nexus-7 Optical Sensor**\n\nBefore proceeding, ensure the Nexus Controller is properly connected and powered via a suitable power source. Connect the 4-pin JST connector as follows: VCC to positive pin, GND to negative pin, Data to pin 1, and Clock to pin 2.\n\n**Setup and Configuration**\n\n1. Connect the Nexus-7 Optical Sensor to the Nexus Controller.\n2. Run the `sensor_init.sh` script to configure the sensor.\n3. Verify the LED is solid green, indicating the sensor is ready, or blinking red if there was an error.\n\n**Safety Precautions**\n\n- **Calibration**: Avoid exposing the sensor to direct sunlight during calibration, as this may cause optical distortion.\n- **Power Specifications**: Ensure the maximum voltage applied to the sensor does not exceed 5V DC.\n\n**Mounting to a Surface**\n\n- Use an M3 screw to secure the sensor to a mounting surface at the corners, taking care not to overtighten.",
